WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.230
In our Solar System, almost
all the mass is in the Sun.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.420
So the outer planets crawl.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:09.960
Neptune orbits at about
a fifth of Earth's speed.

4
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:14.250
In a spiral galaxy, most of the
light comes from the crowded middle.

5
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.420
So we expect the outer
stars to be slower too.

6
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.620
Measure their speeds
from the Doppler shift,

7
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.640
and the outer stars keep up.

8
00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.690
What is holding them in?

9
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.640
In this mission, you'll work
out how fast stars should orbit,

10
00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.150
from the mass inside their orbit.

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.820
Then you'll read a
galaxy's rotation curve,

12
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.650
and see what it says
about where the mass is.

13
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.590
Your mission: explain what keeps the
outer stars on their fast orbits.
